From edc4dcb3ff4c869b1fd366dd87330751a0de4d9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:27:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: check teleport landing zones with either kind of
 teleport

borg_caution_teleport() returned at once unless the borg had both a
teleport scroll or spell (BI_ATELEPORT) and a teleport staff or
activation (BI_AESCAPE). Its callers in the Destruction and Teleport
Level defences ask it whether teleporting would land safely when the
borg has one or the other, so with only scrolls, or only a staff, the
check never ran and the borg cast Destruction or Teleport Level instead
of teleporting to a safe landing.

Require either ability, not both.
---
 src/borg/borg-escape.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-escape.c b/src/borg/borg-escape.c
index 1a77bc61b..1d6ebeb57 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-escape.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-escape.c
@@ -428,8 +428,9 @@ bool borg_caution_teleport(int emergency, int turns)
     q_x = w_x / borg_panel_wid();
     q_y = w_y / borg_panel_hgt();
 
-    /* must have the ability */
-    if (!borg.trait[BI_ATELEPORT] || !borg.trait[BI_AESCAPE])
+    /* must have the ability: a teleport scroll or spell, or a teleport
+     * staff or activation */
+    if (!borg.trait[BI_ATELEPORT] && !borg.trait[BI_AESCAPE])
         return false;
 
     /* Simulate 100 attempts */
